@begin(section)

@title(Changelog)

All notable changes to dsolv are documented in this section. The canonical,
up-to-date changelog lives in the repository's @c(CHANGELOG.md).

@begin(section)
@title(0.2.0 — 2026-08-09)

Added:

@begin(list)
@item(Install-graph output fidelity: JSON and NRDL install-graph entries (and
the JSON packages list) now include each package's @c(requirements) and
@c(metadata) fields, matching legacy degasolv. Present packages serialize
@c(requirements) as JSON @c(null) while resolved packages with no
dependencies serialize @c([]).)
@item(@c(scripts/build): builds the executable with @c(dynamic-space-size=8192)
and @c(control-stack-size=64) baked into the dumped image (overridable via
@c(DYNAMIC_SPACE_SIZE)/@c(CONTROL_STACK_SIZE)).)
@item(No-regex APT parser: @c(slurp-apt-repo) now parses @c(Packages.gz) with
simple line-based operations instead of regular expressions, fixing heap
exhaustion on the 19 MB Ubuntu index. Adds @c(file://) repository URL support
so local index files work.)
@item(The @c(subproc) package system slurper (@c(make-slurper)): runs an
external executable, parses its JSON or NRDL output, and converts it into
resolver query functions. Includes tests for JSON/NRDL parsing, non-zero exit
handling, and unknown output formats.)
@item(Regression tests for the @c(generate-repo-index) to
@c(slurp-degasolv-repo) round trip.)
@end(list)

Fixed:

@begin(list)
@item(Config-file merge precedence: user-specified @c(-c)/@c(-j) config files
now override one another (later files win, matching degasolv's @c(reduce
merge)) while CLI/env values still take precedence.)
@item(Parsed packages with no requirements now carry an empty requirement
list, so JSON output can distinguish present packages (@c(null)) from
resolved packages without dependencies (@c([])).)
@item(@c(generate-repo-index) card decoding: generated repository indexes now
store @c(package-info) structs instead of raw fset maps, so index sort orders
and downstream decoders (@c(slurp-degasolv-repo)) no longer crash.)
@item(@c(query-repo) exit status: a query with no results now exits non-zero
(65, @c(:data-format-error)) as legacy degasolv did.)
@item(Strategy option validation: @c(--search-strat), @c(--conflict-strat),
@c(--list-strat), @c(--resolve-strat), and @c(--index-strat) reject values
other than the legacy degasolv choices with a clean error message.)
@item(@c(resolve-locations) exit status: successful resolutions now exit 0
instead of falling through to the error path and exiting with status 71.)
@item(The @c(subproc) package system's required argument is registered under
the keyword @c(:subproc-exe) so the CLI's required-argument check works.)
@end(list)

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(0.1.0 — 2025-07-31)

Added:

@begin(list)
@item(Initial port of the degasolv dependency resolver from Clojure to Common
Lisp.)
@item(Core resolver data structures and algorithm: @c(package-info),
@c(requirement), @c(version-predicate), @c(decorated-requirement) structs,
string-to-requirement parser, version comparison, spec-calling, and the full
@c(resolve-dependencies-deluxe) algorithm with all strategies (thorough/fast,
exclusive/inclusive/prioritized, breadth-first/depth-first).)
@item(CLI interface using CLIFF with subcommands: @c(display-config),
@c(generate-card), @c(generate-repo-index), @c(resolve-locations),
@c(query-repo).)
@item(Utility functions: @c(data-slurp) (HTTP/file/stdin), @c(base-slurp),
@c(default-spit), @c(pretty-spit), @c(map-query), @c(priority-repo),
@c(global-repo), @c(aggregator).)
@item(Package system modules: core (@c(read-card),
@c(generate-repo-index), @c(slurp-degasolv-repo)), APT
(@c(slurp-apt-repo)), Git (stub), and subproc (@c(make-slurper)).)
@item(ASDF system definition (@c(com.djhaskin.dsolv.asd)) and Roswell script
(@c(com.djhaskin.dsolv.ros)) for executable building.)
@end(list)

@end(section)

@end(section)
